{"mission_id":"0xd4404983d2599a8b0b6fdf57e62f83f24c0fe1aa0862ca3e67e2fef86f62ee78","profile":{"id":"solar-farm","title":"Solar farm O&M survey","ui":{"labels":{"cracked_cell":{"name":"Cracked cell","color":"#ff8a3d"},"soiling":{"name":"Soiling","color":"#b5b0a6"},"unsure":{"name":"Unsure","color":"#ffd60a"}},"skin":"solar"},"decision":{"labels":["cracked_cell","soiling","unsure"],"actions":["descend","continue"],"severity_max":3,"label_actions":{"cracked_cell":"descend","soiling":"continue","unsure":"descend"},"prompt":"You are the sealed decision model of Blackbox, an autonomous solar-farm inspection drone.\nThe image is a top-down RGB camera crop of photovoltaic modules: dark blue cells with thin silver busbars and an aluminium frame. The on-board detector flagged it because part of the crop differs from a clean module. Decide what it is.\n- \"cracked_cell\": physical damage to the glass or cells: bright, sharp, branching or radiating fracture lines, a shattered impact point, or a burn mark. Needs a close-up for the repair crew.\n- \"soiling\": dust, sand, bird droppings, leaves or similar dirt lying on an intact module: soft-edged, brownish or whitish patches. Only needs the cleaning crew.\n- \"unsure\": you cannot tell.\nseverity: integer 0-3 (0 none, 1 single cell, 2 several cells, 3 module-wide). Use 0 for soiling.\naction: \"descend\" to inspect closely (cracked_cell, and unsure), \"continue\" to skip (soiling).\nReply with exactly one JSON object and nothing else, copying the nonce from the user message exactly:\n{\"nonce\":\"<nonce>\",\"label\":\"cracked_cell|soiling|unsure\",\"severity\":0,\"action\":\"descend|continue\"}"}},"model":"qwen3-vl-plus","attestation":"none","chain":{"chain_id":16602,"registry":"0x8d2793615Cb9953c451eecc065a23FfAaBA777a3","register_tx":"0xb3dd026850a44782c7277f2fb78b33cabe48e55412d75e6fd6176fa736eef0ea","close_tx":"0x9a4ce27a312131ff012b74fc8dd72f8da8d6e37e9604495a2c90f6d4bb70d3e4","anchors":["0x5bf568050260f8de9612deb4a6c8d8d8c